  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program for Open and Sustainable Carbon Markets in Lao PDR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program for Open and Sustainable Carbon Markets has been implemented by the Global Green Growth Institute (GGGI) since 2023 with financial support from the Australian Government&#x2019;s Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT). The Project supports the Government of Lao PDR (GoL), particularly the Ministry of Agriculture and Environment (MAE) and the Ministry of Industry and Commerce (MOIC), to enhance access to and participation in international carbon markets under Article 6 of the Paris Agreement. It also supports the development of the energy sector&#x2019;s third Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC3.0) and the integration of carbon markets into the NDC process. Overall, the Project aims to mobilize financial and technological resources for Lao PDR through high-integrity carbon markets and strengthen climate ambition.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to the create a coordinated multi-sectoral framework for sustainable participation in international carbon markets in Lao PDR, in order to increase flows of carbon finance into Lao PDR, facilitating carbon sequestration and emissions reduction projects while aligning with the broader climate policy architecture.</narrative>
  </description>
